BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life of Chuck
DTSTART:20250623T230000Z
DTEND:20250624T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20250623T230000Z
UID:Z6wNiSkq3a
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nFrom the hearts and minds of Ste
 phen King and Mike Flanagan comes The Life of Chuck\, the extraordinary st
 ory of an ordinary man. This unforgettable\, genre-bending tale celebrates
  the life of Charles 'Chuck' Krantz as he experiences the wonder of love\,
  the heartbreak of loss\, and the multitudes contained in all of us. Toro
 nto International Film Festival 2024 People's Choice Award winner.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/life-of-chuck
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brokeback Mountain
DTSTART:20250624T020000Z
DTEND:20250624T043500Z
DTSTAMP:20250624T020000Z
UID:KecBedr52y
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 134 mins (2h14m)\n\n“I wish I knew how to quit you
 .” Celebrate 20 years of Brokeback Mountain with SIFF. Ang Lee’s haunt
 ing\, tender story of forbidden love between two cowboys brought to life b
 y unforgettable performances from Heath Ledger and Jake Gyllenhaal\, was n
 othing short of revolutionary. A turning point for queer cinema and a land
 mark in American film\, Brokeback Mountain continues to move and challenge
  audiences two decades later. See it on the big screen while you can.\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/brokeback-mountain
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All That Jazz
DTSTART:20250703T010000Z
DTEND:20250703T032500Z
DTSTAMP:20250703T010000Z
UID:vajHn3JlNb
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 123 mins (2h03m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club Director/choreog
 rapher Bob Fosse tells his own life story as he details the sordid life of
  Joe Gideon (Roy Scheider)\, a womanizing\, drug-using dancer.\n\nhttps://
 www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/all-that-jazz
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Know Your Place
DTSTART:20250706T020000Z
DTEND:20250706T042000Z
DTSTAMP:20250706T020000Z
UID:x5AjVwWeUZ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nSeattle’s issues with gentrifi
 cation and its impact on our East African community are explored as two te
 enage boys navigate the city to deliver a crucial and time-sensitive packa
 ge to a friend. 2022 Seattle International Film Festival Golden Space Need
 le Award - Best Film. Director Zia Mohajerjasbi scheduled to attend for p
 ost-film Q&A.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/know-your-place
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unstoppable
DTSTART:20250706T193000Z
DTEND:20250706T211500Z
DTSTAMP:20250706T193000Z
UID:fbNNIGdsIM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nSlamdance Unstoppable: On the Roa
 d A showcase of short films made by filmmakers with visible and non-visibl
 e disabilities. Programmed exclusively by disabled artists\, Slamdance Uns
 toppable: On the Road aims to eliminate the prejudices and gate-keeping th
 at have historically kept disabled filmmakers from being represented in th
 e entertainment industry. View From the Floor directors Megan Griffiths a
 nd Mindie Lind scheduled to attend for post-screening Q&A.\n\nhttps://www.
 siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/slamdance-unstoppable-on-the-road/unstoppable-
 shorts
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unstoppable Complicated
DTSTART:20250706T233000Z
DTEND:20250707T011500Z
DTSTAMP:20250706T233000Z
UID:eyLAaUO8Ka
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 83 mins (1h23m)\n\nSlamdance Unstoppable: On the Roa
 d In a failing healthcare system\, children with complex\, invisible illne
 ss and their families are labeled “too complicated” or torn apart by a
 ccusations of medical child abuse. Documentary feature.\n\nhttps://www.sif
 f.net/cinema/in-theaters/slamdance-unstoppable-on-the-road/complicated
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
